# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# D'YVIX IT Solutions — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. Never commit .env.local.
# No secret is required to run the site; the variables below tune behaviour
# and enable enquiry delivery.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The canonical origin is not an environment variable: it is site.url in
# src/lib/site.ts, used for canonical URLs, Open Graph, sitemap and JSON-LD.

# --- Enquiry form rate limiting -------------------------------------------
# Fixed window, applied per client IP, held in process memory.
# NOTE: on a multi-instance or serverless deployment each instance keeps its
# own counter, so the effective limit is per instance. Move to a shared store
# (Redis / Upstash) before relying on this for anything security-critical.
RATE_LIMIT_MAX="5"
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS="60000"

# --- Enquiry delivery by e-mail (SMTP) ------------------------------------
# Each enquiry is sent to the team from a mailbox on the host. On cPanel,
# Email Accounts -> Connect Devices lists these values; set them in Setup
# Node.js App -> Environment variables (docs/deploiement-cpanel.md, step 7).
# Server-side only: never add the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Until they are set,
# the form tells visitors it could not send and to email directly.
#
# Port 465 uses TLS from the first byte; any other port must offer STARTTLS.
# SMTP_HOST="mail.dyvixitsolutions.com"
# SMTP_PORT="465"
# SMTP_USER="site@dyvixitsolutions.com"
# SMTP_PASS=""
#
# Optional: who receives enquiries (default: contact@dyvixitsolutions.com).
# ENQUIRY_TO_EMAIL="contact@dyvixitsolutions.com"
#
# Local development without a real mailbox: run the test sink
# (node e2e/support/smtp-sink.mjs), then use SMTP_HOST=127.0.0.1,
# SMTP_PORT=2525 and the user and password from e2e/support/sink.json.
# What it receives is listed at http://127.0.0.1:2526/messages.
